<html><body><p>lea-proxy: %H refused: it is not in the egress allowlist (LEA_EGRESS_ALLOW). To reach it, add its domain to LEA_EGRESS_ALLOW in ~/.config/lea/lea.conf (comma separated; a domain covers its subdomains; "default" keeps lea's default list, as in LEA_EGRESS_ALLOW="default,example.com"), then run lea stop --all and start lea again: the proxy restarts with the new list.</p></body></html>
